WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.3 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Indicators

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
An indicator is a clearly defined sign that shows whether a result is happening.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Define it so two people measure it alike.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Give every percentage a numerator and denominator.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Break data down to see who is missed.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“First-check rejection rate: pieces rejected divided by pieces checked each month, by village and years weaving.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You create an indicator reference sheet for your priority results.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
